==Battleground==
*1 [[Mr. Mer]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Mole]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Dober P.D]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns.
**1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage consists of a timed [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] phase and a base-hit [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] phase, therefore it's best to bring a lineup that can handle both of these enemy types. For the first phase, [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune units]] like [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Dancer]] are the best option since both Mer and Dober have [[Wave Attack|Wave Attacks/Mini-Waves]]. [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]], and [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] can also be useful in controlling the initial Traitless enemies. Note that you should try your best to defeat Mr. Mole before you hit the base, as his high health and knockback count can easily keep him alive well into the second segment of the stage and make it difficult. In the second section, you can use [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]] and stallers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]], [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]] or [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy]] on Boraphim, but be sure to have multiple meatshields to deal with Cala Maria. On higher crown difficulties, [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] is a great option for the beginning segment. [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] also works against if you have him unlocked by the time you do 4* difficulty. [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] is a great choice for both sections of this stage, as he is a spammable meatshield for Cala Maria, has a Research [[Cat Combo|Combo]] that can make Ramen Cat more spammable, and can even become Immune to Waves with Talents, all while being the cheapest meatshield in the game.

==Trivia==
*The "Disaster" in Disaster Cycle may be a hint towards the stage having [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] that was lost in translation. It was translated from 天変地異 ''tenpenchii'', an idiom that refers to a catastrophic natural disaster, but contains 天, a kanji meaning heaven/sky.

